@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Camera Frame" as Frame
rectangle "PoseObservation\nMediaPipe output only; no image bytes" as PoseObs
rectangle "Telemetry Sampler + Chunker" as TelemetryStage
rectangle "PoseObservationChunk\nversioned binary payload" as PoseChunk
rectangle "Tracking / Calibration Debug Events" as Tracking
rectangle "Rep Metrics" as Metrics
rectangle "Set-scoped FormEvent + FormEvidence[]\noptional repId" as Events
rectangle "CueDelivery\nactual feedback only" as CueDelivery
rectangle "CompactRepTrace\n+ generic TraceChannel[]" as CompactTrace
rectangle "Daily Nutrition Context" as Nutrition
rectangle "DailyHealthSummary" as DailyHealth
rectangle "WeeklyBodyComposition" as Weekly
rectangle "Health Connect Fine-grained Records\nprocessing input only" as Health
rectangle "Health Aggregator\nin-memory" as HealthAgg
rectangle "Debug Video\nopt-in only" as Video
queue "Short-lived Telemetry Buffer\nbest-effort" as TelemetryQ
queue "Priority Persistence Queue" as PriorityQ
rectangle "Batch Writer" as Writer
rectangle "Retention Worker\nstartup + periodic" as Retention
rectangle "Startup Recovery" as Recovery
database "Room / SQLite" as Room
rectangle "App-private no-backup storage" as Files

Frame --> PoseObs : pose inference output
Frame --> Video : explicit debug mode only
Frame --> Frame : discard immediately
PoseObs --> TelemetryStage : candidate observation
TelemetryStage --> PoseChunk : bounded-rate sample + chunk encode
PoseChunk --> TelemetryQ : short-lived chunk
Tracking --> TelemetryQ : short-lived debug events
Metrics --> PriorityQ : long-term derived metrics
Events --> PriorityQ : structured detected issue episodes
CueDelivery --> PriorityQ : actual feedback record
CompactTrace --> PriorityQ : long-term generic compact trace
PriorityQ --> Writer : priority batches
TelemetryQ --> Writer : best-effort short-lived batches
Writer --> Room

Nutrition --> Room : long-term compact daily context
Health --> HealthAgg : normalize / aggregate
HealthAgg --> DailyHealth : daily compact summary
HealthAgg --> Weekly : weekly medians + counts
DailyHealth --> Room : long-term
Weekly --> Room : long-term
HealthAgg --> HealthAgg : discard fine-grained inputs
Video --> Files : <= 7 days
Retention --> Room : prune expired set-scoped chunks/events
Retention --> Files : delete expired debug media
Recovery --> Room : stale ACTIVE hierarchy/events -> INTERRUPTED

note right of TelemetryStage
Realtime inference rate and persisted telemetry rate are independent.
Chunk multiple timestamped observations into a versioned binary payload.
Exact sample rate, chunk size and codec belong in SPEC/tests.
end note

note right of PoseChunk
Do not store one Room row per analyzed frame.
Chunks are short-lived, set-scoped and logically expire at
ExerciseSet.telemetryExpiresAt.
end note

note right of Tracking
Emit meaningful state transitions rather than every bad frame.
Tracking/calibration debug events share the set's short-lived expiry.
end note

note right of Events
One continuous detected problem is one FormEvent episode.
Activation/finalization update the same id; CueDelivery is separate.
end note

note right of CompactTrace
Keep a small generic standardized trace long-term.
Use schemaId + typed channels for exercise-specific signals.
This supports longitudinal reinterpretation, not full raw replay.
end note

note bottom of PriorityQ
This queue prioritizes persistence but is not itself durable.
Durability begins at successful Room commit.
Normal Stop Set uses a reserved SetCloseBarrier after all earlier
high-value records and in-memory analyzer/rule finalization.
end note

note bottom of Retention
Logical expiry occurs at ExerciseSet.telemetryExpiresAt.
Expired short-lived rows are excluded from normal reads immediately.
Physical deletion occurs on startup/periodic local cleanup.
end note

note bottom of Recovery
If the process dies with ACTIVE workout/execution/set/FormEvent records,
startup recovery marks them INTERRUPTED instead of leaving open history.
end note

note bottom of Room
Real personal data stays on-device only.
Android cloud backup disabled; no export/share in MVP.
end note

@enduml
